# Styling: Tailwind only (hard)

**All layout and visual styling uses Tailwind utility classes.** Custom CSS and `style=` are banned for layout, spacing, color, typography, borders, shadows, sizing, and z-index.

## Banned (absolute)

- Building CSS strings in `<script>` (`$derived`, `.join()`, template literals) and binding them to `style=`
- `style=` / `style:` for height, width, padding, margin, gap, z-index, color, font, border, shadow, display, position (except true one-off animation progress driven by runtime values)
- Component-specific CSS classes in `app.css` (or elsewhere) that Tailwind utilities already cover
- TS constants whose only purpose is feeding those layout styles (`APP_HEADER_HEIGHT_PX`, etc.)

```svelte
<!-- BAD -->
const headerStyle = $derived(
	[
		`height: ${APP_HEADER_HEIGHT_PX}px`,
		`padding: 0 ${APP_HEADER_HORIZONTAL_PADDING_PX}px`,
		`gap: ${APP_HEADER_SECTION_GAP_PX}px`,
		`z-index: ${APP_HEADER_Z_INDEX}`
	].join('; ')
);
<header style={headerStyle}>…</header>
```

```svelte
<!-- GOOD -->
<header class="sticky top-0 z-header flex h-16 items-center gap-8 px-6 shadow-(--header-shadow)">…</header>
```

Prefer theme utilities (`rounded`, `z-header`) and Tailwind v4 canonical token classes (`outline-(--ring)`, `text-(--foreground)`). Ban `*[var(--token)]` when `*(--token)` or a named utility works.

Use `cn()` with **one concern per argument** (position → layout → type → color → motion → interactive → state). Do not dump every utility into a single string.

## Allowed CSS only for

- `@keyframes` / animation definitions and `prefers-reduced-motion` companions
- Global design tokens in `@theme` / `:root` (colors, fonts, radii, shadows) consumed by Tailwind — not component layout rules
- Third-party / shadcn primitive styles that the stack already ships

If a visual need feels “hard in Tailwind,” prefer theme tokens + utilities (`h-16`, `px-6`, `gap-8`, `shadow-(--header-shadow)`) over new CSS or `style=`. Full text: [`docs/code-rules.md`](../../docs/code-rules.md).
